WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.034
What separates the great funds from the mediocre ones?

00:00:03.274 --> 00:00:08.094
It is not investment judgement alone. It is
how they grow their next set of leaders.

00:00:08.694 --> 00:00:14.281
Judgement lives in people. In a study of nearly
4,000 buyout managers, the individual

00:00:14.281 --> 00:00:18.751
mattered about four times as much as
the firm in explaining returns.

00:00:18.991 --> 00:00:22.569
And when senior partners leave, raising
the next fund gets harder.

00:00:22.809 --> 00:00:25.716
Leadership is what turns a fund into an institution.

00:00:26.316 --> 00:00:30.490
Yet most private equity firms have never
written down their craft, what

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:34.134
it takes to lead an investment fund, competency by competency.

00:00:34.374 --> 00:00:40.140
And few help each leader trace their arc, the progress
they make on every competency their craft demands.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:45.213
So the craft stays in a few heads, and feedback
arrives once a year, too late to use.

00:00:45.813 --> 00:00:50.164
That is why we built CraftArc, to help
funds build their next set of leaders.

00:00:50.404 --> 00:00:56.441
It tracks how each leader is progressing, on investment
judgement and on fit with your people and culture.

00:00:57.041 --> 00:01:00.918
And it gives you one view of your whole
senior team, person by person.

00:01:01.518 --> 00:01:05.341
Here is why it works. First, we bring
the expertise to frame your

00:01:05.341 --> 00:01:09.165
competency model with you, so your
craft is finally written down.

00:01:09.405 --> 00:01:14.790
Second, it removes the administrative burden.
An AI agent holds the conversations,

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:18.665
gathers the feedback in one place and drafts the write-ups.

00:01:18.905 --> 00:01:22.313
Third, each person owns their development plan and tracks it.

00:01:22.553 --> 00:01:26.803
So your partners spend their time grooming
leaders instead of chasing feedback.

00:01:27.403 --> 00:01:31.816
The agent is an expert in conversation.
Here is how a cycle unfolds.

00:01:32.056 --> 00:01:38.087
It talks with each person for their self-evaluation,
by voice or text, in about 25 minutes.

00:01:38.327 --> 00:01:43.839
It helps the evaluator design the feedback interviews,
so the right people speak to each competency.

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:48.505
It speaks with each contributor, and gathers
what they saw first-hand in one place.

00:01:48.745 --> 00:01:53.812
It drafts the memo for your Executive Committee,
and the evaluator owns the final wording.

00:01:54.052 --> 00:01:58.614
And it helps each person build their own development
plan, then track it through the year.

00:01:58.854 --> 00:02:02.979
Five conversations make one arc, and
every leader knows where they stand.

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:07.799
If your next review cycle starts in the
new year, now is the time to set it up.

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:11.114
To book a demo, write to dash@craftarc.ai.

00:02:11.354 --> 00:02:13.215
This voice is AI generated.
